__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store

# Environments and local secrets
.pixi/
.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated outputs
output/
outputs/
results/
# ENDO-TWIN results are committed (regenerated by `pixi run endotwin-all`)
!endotwin/results/
logs/
tmp/
chatgpt_results_with_figures.tar.gz

# Source evidence is local-only from 2026-11-23 on.
#
# This repository has a PUBLIC GitHub remote, and data/ holds material that is
# not ours to redistribute: three publisher PDFs, the Zaragozano manuscript and
# supplementary .docx files, and the secreted-protein workbook. The MIT licence
# in LICENSE covers this repository's own code and documentation, never these
# files. Everything under data/ is therefore untracked, extending the rule that
# already applied to the RDS and the annotation workbook below.
#
# What does NOT change: data/ stays the immutable source layer (AGENTS.md), the
# files stay on the machines that have them, and config/data_manifest.tsv keeps
# pinning every one by SHA-256. Copies committed before 2026-11-23 remain in the
# Git history and on the public remote; untracking does not retract them.
#
# Accepted consequence, already true for the two paths below: a fresh clone
# cannot pass check_data_manifest.py --check-hashes, and the prototype tests
# that read data/ need the files restored out of band. The ENDO-TWIN mainline
# (src/endotwin, tests/mainline, endotwin/) reads nothing under data/ and is
# unaffected.
# `data/*`, not `data/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# bare `data/` would make the negation below unreachable.
data/*
# The directory's own documentation carries no third-party content and tells a
# clone what belongs here, so it stays tracked.
!data/README.md

# MaBoSS generated artifacts
*.probtraj.csv
*.statdist.csv
*.fp.csv
*.run.log

# Literature PDFs: never committed. Only extracted, attributed
# claim-level assertions and bibliographic records belong in the repo.
context/literature/pdfs/
context/literature/supplements/

# Local-only annotation source. Manifested in config/data_manifest.tsv and
# pinned by sha256 -- exactly like the RDS above -- but never committed:
# xl/sharedStrings.xml carries the lab's own cell-source codes and a collection
# date, and this repository has a shared GitHub remote and an external-bundle
# export path (src/scripts/make_chatgpt_results_bundle.sh copies config/, context/,
# docs/ and input_tables/). Only opaque repository-local donor-group labels plus
# source-cell coordinates are committed; the crosswalk deliberately does not
# exist here. See config/source_contract.yaml local_only_verification.
#
# Accepted consequence: a clone without this file cannot pass
# check_data_manifest.py --check-hashes. Already true for the RDS above.
# Path is NFC -- an editor normalizing it to NFD silently stops matching.
data/secreción proteinas ADOC anotaciones.xlsx

# Local editor settings, not part of the project contract.
.vscode/
